<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Questions to ask before you pay</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>What exactly will be done this month?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>How will I see the work: links, a change log, a report?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Who does the work?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Is there a contract, and how do I stop?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>What do you need from me?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>What will you not promise?</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Warning signs</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>A guaranteed position on Google. Nobody controls Google.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Hundreds of links for very little money. These are usually automated and can do harm.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>A long contract before any work has been shown.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Reports full of charts with no list of tasks.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Being asked for your passwords.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where to start on a small budget</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pick the one job most likely to matter. For a local trade, that is usually your Google Business Profile and directory listings. For a site that gets visitors but few enquiries, it is the pages themselves. If you do not know what is wrong, an audit tells you where to spend first.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:group {"className":"ifm-faq","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ifm-faq"><!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Is cheap SEO a waste of money?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not if it is a clearly defined job done properly. Be suspicious when a low price is attached to a big promise.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Do I have to pay every month?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>No. One-off jobs such as an audit or a profile clean-up are useful by themselves. Ongoing work helps most in competitive markets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>How long until it pays for itself?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It varies with your market. Some changes show within weeks, and most SEO builds over several months.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details -->

<!-- wp:details -->
<details class="wp-block-details"><summary>Can I do it myself?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Much of it, yes, if you have the time. Our guides cover the basics, and a consultation can give you a plan to follow.</p>
